# E05 English auction with broadcast: sequential, fixed order; the valuations come from the seed of the oracle, so the
# C# fixes every line (exact trace), the dots of the bids the bidders hear included: a dot has no line break, so the next
# line of the auctioneer follows the dots on the same line. "line" checks the whole trace, the other facts each kind.
cover all
fact line ^(.*)$
fact valuation ^\[(bidder\d+)\]: My valuation is (\d+)$
fact start ^\t\[auctioneer -> (bidder\d+)\]: start$
fact bid ^\.*\t\[(bidder\d+) -> auctioneer\]: bid (\d+)$
fact finished ^\.*\[auctioneer\]: Auction finished$
fact winner ^\t\[auctioneer -> (bidder\d+)\]: winner (\w+)$
fact won ^\[(bidder\d+)\]: I have won with (\d+)$
same line seq
same valuation seq
same start seq
same bid seq
same winner seq
same won seq
check valuation count == 5
check finished count == 1
check won count == 1
